  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1123 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nDangerous heat expected again Tuesday before a minor cool down by\nWednesday. Convection will approach the forecast area by Tuesday\nevening but struggle to make a more southward advance. A weak cold\nfront will gradually push south and westward into the forecast\narea and become a zone for a chance of showers and storms Tuesday\nnight into Wednesday primarily across far E OK and NW AR.\n\nTemperatures and dewpoint trends along and west of the weak\nboundary will be challenge as potential for moisture pooling may\noffset the minor cool down and still result in excessive heat\nindex values on Wednesday. \n\nThe overall pattern will see the upper ridge become centered more\nwestward by late week and temperatures will likely trend toward\nmore seasonal normals. There could also be an increase in shower\nand storm chances the region aligns on the periphery of the upper\nridge but uncertainty remains high.",
